  <Card eyebrow="04 / slash commands for claude" title="What the agent can call">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-4 max-w-3xl">
      Slash commands wrap the chassis scripts so the agent doesn't need to
      remember bash invocations. The chassis surfaces them in every turn's
      injection reminder.
    </p>
    <table class="w-full font-mono text-xs border-2 border-border">
      <thead class="bg-[var(--surface-1)] border-b-2 border-border">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-3 py-2 w-48">slash</th>
          <th class="text-left px-3 py-2">when to call</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/whatknows &lt;path&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Before opening any code file — answers "what do we already know about this?"</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/cite &lt;symbol&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Mid-task: a symbol shows up, grep all layers for it</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/find &lt;natural-q&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">BM25 retrieval when prompt wording differs from note titles</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/queue</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">"What is the chassis asking me to review?"</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/revise &lt;topic&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Topic note disagrees with code you just read — pre-stages diffs</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/promote &lt;tag&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">≥3 episodes share a tag — distill into a topic note</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/episode &lt;title&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Manual episode (preempts the auto-draft)</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/seam &lt;a&gt; &lt;b&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Record a cross-repo edge</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/gap-scan &lt;repo&gt; &lt;slug&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Survey an external ecosystem, ground it against one of our libs, emit a prioritized build backlog</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/analyze-paper &lt;repo&gt; &lt;slug&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Deep-analyze a paper into an implementable-concept topic note for a target lib</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/propose &lt;repo&gt; &lt;slug&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Turn gaps + papers + trends into an investment-thesis-backed build proposal (can propose a new repo)</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/proposal-final-draft &lt;slug&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Render a finalized proposal into a formal proposal document</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/orient</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Force re-inject for current cwd</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/freshness</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Per-repo fetch age + drift status</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/stack</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Show the branch stack tree (uses git-spice if installed)</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/stack-new &lt;slug&gt;</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Start a new branch on top of HEAD with parent tracking</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/stack-pr</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Push current branch + open/update its PR</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)] bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/stack-submit</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Push every branch in the stack + open/update each PR</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-soft)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/stack-restack</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Cascade-rebase descendants after a parent moved</td></tr>
        <tr class="bg-[var(--surface-1)]"><td class="px-3 py-2 text-accent">/stack-sync</td><td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">Pull main + cascade-rebase whole stack (post-merge recovery)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Card>

  <Card eyebrow="05 / MCP tools" title="What the agent can call mid-loop (without a slash)">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-3 max-w-3xl">
      Slashes are one-shot. MCP tools are callable inside any turn — the
      cartograph MCP server exposes three augmenting tools (no wrapping of
      <code>Read</code> / <code>Grep</code>):
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 max-w-3xl text-sm">
      <li><code class="text-accent">cartograph_search(query, repo?, layer?, k=10)</code> — BM25 ranked retrieval. Call before grepping.</li>
      <li><code class="text-accent">cartograph_notes_for_file(path)</code> — reverse index. Call before <code>Read</code> of any workspace file.</li>
      <li><code class="text-accent">cartograph_drift(repo, anchor?)</code> — drift state. Call before trusting any topic note.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-3 max-w-3xl">
      Enable per-project by creating <code>.mcp.json</code> at the cartograph
      root with the server entry — see
      <code>claude-designs/cartograph/mcp-surface/</code>. The classifier blocks
      the agent from authoring this file itself; opt-in is by the human.
    </p>
  </Card>

  <Card eyebrow="06 / example scenarios" title="How Claude agents actually use this">
    <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div>
        <div class="font-bold mb-1">Scenario A — "Why is my checkpoint save hanging on multi-host?"</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">
          User opens Claude in <code>workspace/orbax/</code>. The
          <code>UserPromptSubmit</code> hook fires: bedrock + topics injected;
          BM25 surfaces <code>guides/orbax/topics/multi-host-coordination.md</code>
          and <code>guides/orbax/topics/async-checkpoint-flow.md</code> (scores
          13.5 / 8.6); path-token lookup finds <code>async_checkpointer.py</code>
          notes. Agent reads the topic notes <em>before</em> opening upstream
          code. If a claim contradicts what the code now shows, <code>/revise
          async-checkpoint-flow</code> pre-stages diffs and the agent revises
          the topic in place. Stop hook auto-drafts an episode if anything new
          was learned.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="font-bold mb-1">Scenario B — Stacked PR cascade after #1 merges</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">
          The user is on stack <code>bench-1 → bench-2 → ... → bench-7</code>.
          PR #1 just merged. Agent calls <code>/stack-sync</code>:
          git-spice pulls main, deletes the merged <code>bench-1</code>
          locally, then cascade-rebases <code>bench-2..7</code> onto the new
          main. Conflicts surface inline — agent resolves them with normal
          <code>git add</code> + <code>git rebase --continue</code> and re-runs.
          Then <code>/stack-submit</code> force-pushes every updated branch
          with <code>--force-with-lease</code>. Throughout, the
          <a href="/prs/" class="text-accent hover:underline">/prs/</a> page
          shows live status across all eight upstreams.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="font-bold mb-1">Scenario C — Random Friday: "what's been happening?"</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">
          User opens cartograph cold. Home shows: 3 auto-drafted episodes
          awaiting review (the chassis caught them at session-end), 1 per-repo
          drift report opened on jax (4 commits ahead), 2 topic-level drifts
          on orbax (cited code refactored). User clicks
          <a href="/console/review/" class="text-accent hover:underline">/console/review/</a>
          to triage the auto-drafted episodes — bless the good ones, reject
          the noisy one with a note (which triggers
          <code>revise-rejected.sh</code> to refine it). Then to
          <a href="/diary/" class="text-accent hover:underline">/diary/</a>
          to read what the chassis did while they were away.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="font-bold mb-1">Scenario D — Reading a paper that informs a design</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">
          Agent in <code>workspace/orbax/</code> consults a safetensors paper
          via WebFetch. Stop hook detects the external lookup and auto-drafts a
          <code>papers/orbax/&lt;slug&gt;/notes.md</code>. The note lands with
          <code>auto_drafted: true</code> and shows up on
          <a href="/console/review/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Review</a>
          alongside auto-drafted episodes. User reviews, blesses, and the paper
          becomes part of the corpus — searchable via BM25, discoverable via
          Library facets.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Card>

  <Card eyebrow="07 / discipline" title="The one rule that makes it compound">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted max-w-3xl mb-3">
      Cartograph gets <em>better</em> over time (not just <em>bigger</em>) because
      of one rule:
    </p>
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[var(--accent)] pl-4 italic text-fg max-w-3xl">
      When a topic note disagrees with the code you just read, <strong>revise it
      in place</strong>. Bump <code>last_revised</code>. Write a short episode
      recording what changed and why.
    </blockquote>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted max-w-3xl mt-3">
      Don't fork a new file with a similar slug. Don't add a "## YYYY-MM-DD
      update" if the original is now wrong. Edit the source. Bedrock is three
      files per repo, ever. Topic notes are one slug per topic. Revision &gt;
      accumulation — every other rule is downstream of this one.
    </p>
  </Card>

